@page "/"

<PageTitle>Denny Kim · Design OS</PageTitle>

<div class="pf-hero">
    <h1>Design that ships as working software.</h1>
    <p>
        I'm Denny Kim, a UX/UI designer at SimplePart (9 years). Instead of handing developers
        static mockups, I build functioning Blazor prototypes that mirror our production
        component structure — so design decisions arrive as code, not pictures of code.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="pf-section">
    <h2>Start here</h2>
    <div class="pf-cards">
        <a class="pf-card" href="workshop">
            <span class="pf-tag">38 components · live</span>
            <h3>Component workshop</h3>
            <p>The real Blazor storefront components I built, running against dummy data. Pick a vehicle, watch them react.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="pf-card" href="build-log">
            <span class="pf-tag">The story</span>
            <h3>Build log</h3>
            <p>How a Sketch-era designer ended up running a .NET component sandbox — and why it changed how design hands off work.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="pf-card" href="experiments">
            <span class="pf-tag">In progress</span>
            <h3>Experiments</h3>
            <p>Agentic commerce, conversational fitment, and checkout UX explorations — prototypes, not slideware.</p>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="pf-section">
    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <div class="pf-cards">
        <div class="pf-card">
            <span class="pf-tag">Method</span>
            <h3>AI-orchestrated development</h3>
            <p>Every component here was built by directing AI coding agents — architecture, review, and UX judgment stayed with me.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-card">
            <span class="pf-tag">Stack</span>
            <h3>Blazor, like production</h3>
            <p>The sandbox mirrors SimplePart's actual direction: .NET with Blazor/Razor components. Prototypes speak the same language as the product.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-card">
            <span class="pf-tag">Data</span>
            <h3>Dummy data throughout</h3>
            <p>One fictional dealer, one make, four models. Nothing here touches real customer or company data.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
